  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...High pressure builds in tonight through \nSaturday bringing clearing skies with cooler and less humid \nconditions. \n\nA cold front still located near the coast will move offshore through \ntonight. Behind the cold front, it looks drier into at least \ntomorrow. A high pressure system builds in for Saturday keeping the \narea dry. An upper-level disturbance moving through the region on \nSunday has the potential to result in some showers and \nthunderstorms, particularly during the afternoon and evening\nhours.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Increasing heat and humidity return next week \nwith unsettled weather.\n\nBroad upper level ridging returns to the eastern US early next week, \nbringing in surface high pressure across the eastern US.\nAfternoon highs will creep back into the upper 80s to low 90s, about \n5 degrees above average for early September. Dew points will also \ncreep back into the low 70s. One other aspect to watch with this\nridging pattern is the potential for thunderstorms to rotate \naround the periphery of the ridge and the position of a warm\nfront next week. The exact location, timing, and intensity of \nthe thunderstorms remains a bit uncertain at this range. \nCurrently, the main days to monitor are Tuesday and Wednesday \nregarding heavy rain and severe weather potential.",
